{
  "about": [
    "English morphology for the matcher (extension/src/matcher.js, scripts/matcher.py; docs/matcher.md), and closed-class",
    "English the extension's validation reads (extension/src/levels.js: joiners, verb_s, polarity).",
    "verbs: irregular verbs, base -> its irregular forms (past, participle, and -s where irregular); -s and -ing are",
    "otherwise made by rule, and a listed verb gets no regular -ed. plurals: irregular plurals, base -> plural forms",
    "(an empty list: the same as the singular). comparatives: irregular comparatives and superlatives; other adjectives",
    "take -er and -est by rule. phrases: English that stands for a gloss without being one of its inflections, phrase",
    "-> the glosses it can stand for (there is -> exist, myself -> self); an entry with such a gloss also matches the",
    "phrase. auxiliaries: \"have\" and \"do\" as helper verbs (have been, did not), which never match a gloss \"have\" or",
    "\"do\": the forms, the next words that make one a helper, whether a participle next does, and the adverbs that may",
    "come between. determiners: words after which a bare verb is a noun (the rest, a look). function: English closed-class",
    "words (pronouns, determiners, prepositions, conjunctions, auxiliaries, numbers and the commonest function adverbs),",
    "which are never inflected by rule and mark a span as a function word for reporting and sense flags.",
    "joiners: English that joins a clause, or a noun, to the rest (subordinating conjunctions and the prepositions that",
    "double as them), whose Japanese comes after what it joins (~toki, ~aida, ~mae, ~ato, ~made, ~kara, ~kedo), so no",
    "word swap may stand in front of what it joins (\"if\" is not one: moshi comes first in Japanese too; \"when\" and",
    "\"where\" asking a question are question words). verb_s: words whose \"'s\" is always \"is\", \"has\" or \"does\", never a",
    "possessive (\"that's\", \"it's\"). polarity: words after which, in the same sentence, \"anything\" or \"anyone\" means any",
    "at all in a negation, condition or comparison (nanika, nanimo), not a free choice (nandemo).",
    "Generated into extension/src/english.js by python3 scripts/matcher.py --js; both tests check they agree."
  ],
